                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a614df0e-33b4-3c1c-ad0d-a216c1195a25",
                        "entry_id": "498b0dfe-2afb-3b12-80b5-660eb4cbc749",
                        "glosses": [
                            "хим. имеющий в строении углеродного скелета два кольца ковалентных связей между атомами (о циклических углеводородах)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "75749bac-c8b6-463f-b7d4-6f8d0a2a28bb",
                                "sense_id": "a614df0e-33b4-3c1c-ad0d-a216c1195a25",
                                "text": "Углеродные атомы, образующие кольцо, могут быть связаны друг с другом дополнительной цепочкой, как бы перебрасывающей между ними мостик. Если такой мостик связывает смежные атомы, то возникающую при этом бициклическую систему называют конденсированной."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bebe310c-3901-46fa-92bb-568443e7a369",
                                "sense_id": "a614df0e-33b4-3c1c-ad0d-a216c1195a25",
                                "text": "Камфора — бициклический кетон."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "12988e36-de75-461a-8e0c-f9f39a697294",
                        "source_entry_id": "498b0dfe-2afb-3b12-80b5-660eb4cbc749",
                        "source_sense_id": "a614df0e-33b4-3c1c-ad0d-a216c1195a25",
                        "target_lang_word": "bicyclic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bicyclic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9c548c20-8c1f-3180-8adb-53dad5d4ded7",
                                        "entry_id": "2185774e-c938-311d-aaf0-f65f17211b46",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having two cycles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0be1577e-917a-3ffd-b976-4de4fb6d1256",
                                        "entry_id": "2185774e-c938-311d-aaf0-f65f17211b46",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having two rings of atoms in the molecule; the rings may be fused, as in naphthalene, or separate, as in biphenyl."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "physical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f72833d5-06b1-46b3-a093-f49b67e33bd5",
                                                "sense_id": "0be1577e-917a-3ffd-b976-4de4fb6d1256",
                                                "text": "[…] substitution of a carboxylate would be expected to destabilize the dritterionic mesomer that contributes to the singlet valence bond description as the benzyne geometry becomes more bicyclic."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c545930-0684-47e4-9ad5-049ae170c5ff",
                                                "sense_id": "0be1577e-917a-3ffd-b976-4de4fb6d1256",
                                                "text": "These geometries are almost reversed in the triplets. The 1,3-borazyne (III) shows more bicyclic character than the corresponding m-benzyne"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "69d888b2-2aa8-4baa-b27b-3eb81769dfc4",
                                                "sense_id": "0be1577e-917a-3ffd-b976-4de4fb6d1256",
                                                "text": "On the basis of a comparison of calculated and measured IR data, the 2 B 2 state could undoubtedly be discarded in favor of a more bicyclic geometry"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "bicyclic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f36e259-ad02-3ea6-93b1-1931e673c772",
                                        "entry_id": "aad9ab85-a81b-305e-afe6-a19fad47d0f3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bicyclic compound."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "physical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
